# Site content width

Every page section, navbar, and footer content column must use the shared site width — never invent a one-off layout max-width.

## Source of truth

- Token: `--max-width-site: 100rem` in `src/styles/index.css` (`@theme`)
- Tailwind: `max-w-site`
- Component: `SiteContainer` from `@/components/layout/SiteContainer`

## Do

```jsx
import SiteContainer from '@/components/layout/SiteContainer'

<section className="bg-foam px-6 py-24">
  <SiteContainer>{/* section content */}</SiteContainer>
</section>
```

- Put horizontal padding on the section or on `SiteContainer` (`px-6 sm:px-8`), not a different max-width
- Prefer `<SiteContainer>` over raw `max-w-site` so structure stays consistent
- Use `as={motion.div}` when the container itself needs Framer Motion props

## Don’t

```jsx
// ❌ BAD — breaks the site grid
<div className="mx-auto max-w-6xl">…
<div className="mx-auto max-w-[90rem]">…

// ✅ GOOD
<SiteContainer>…
```
